  <prompt>
    Author the new `docs/architecture/communication-intelligence-architecture.md` describing the R4 Communication Intelligence layer as-built, using the `docs-architecture` skill. Cover, grounded in the shipped code:

    - The direction-agnostic `ICommunicationEnrichmentService` (both inbound + outbound; ordered pipeline: association → categorization → AI analysis → RAG indexing → Responsive-Intelligence trigger; best-effort/non-fatal invariant).
    - The unified Association Engine over the normalized message envelope (never `Microsoft.Graph.Message`), the rung ladder (0 explicit-ref, 1 thread continuity, 2 participant correlation, 3 structural detectors, 4 semantic `RecordSearchService`, 5 JPS AI extract+classify), per-attribute confidence + provenance, eight target entities.
    - Confidence→status mapping + auto-file (deterministic ≥0.85 → Resolved via ADR-018 kill-switch; AI rungs never auto-file → Suggested/Ambiguous).
    - Channel seams (`ICommunicationChannelSender`/`ICommunicationArchiver`, email-only impl) and the NFR-04 extensibility contract.
    - Responsive Intelligence (OutputRouter record/notification legs → EventRules → CreateEvent/Task/Notification + DeliverComposite Triage summary).
    - Central auth (ADR-028), the Communication Code Page review surface + add-in save-pane consumer, and the retirement of the OOB-`email` subsystem.

    Cross-reference ADR-045 (canonical Communication ADR) and the related ADRs (024/028/018/013/037/015). Keep it a design/rationale doc (WHY + structure), not implementation detail — pointers to code entry points, not code dumps.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Spaarke architecture writer authoritative on the R4 Communication Intelligence subsystem. Uses the `docs-architecture` skill and follows the repo's architecture-doc conventions (decisions + rationale, code entry-point pointers).
  </role>

